From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:04:09 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Plutonium: the dock scrolls, from four slots up, and a
 slot's editor sets its keys
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Four slots by default, up to 24: the slot editor adds one after it or
  removes it (the slots after it move along; keys stay with places).
- Rows of the same length, at least four to a row, as many as fit the
  sidebar, split evenly so rows are full when the count allows (ten where
  eight fit: two rows of five). Past two rows the dock scrolls.
- The editor's Keys: a slot's key, its other-layout key and its put-here
  key, each recorded with a click and saved to keybindings.json. Slots past
  the ninth have commands (dock.slot.10…24 and the rest) but no default key.
- Labels and toasts say the slot's own key, not Super+N.
- A field recording a shortcut gets every key: resolveShortcutCommand
  answers nothing while one has focus.
- Stored dock state version 3: a count, enough for the last slot set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
